    <p>You&rsquo;ll hear that District 7 is &ldquo;the new prime&rdquo;. Some of that is fair. Beach Road sits between Bugis and Marina Bay, and the government has put real plans on the map around it. But &ldquo;prime&rdquo; is a label, not a reason to buy. The questions that matter for your household are simpler: what are you paying per square foot, who else will you be competing with when you sell, and does the quantum fit your finances without stretching them?</p>

    <p>Aurea is not a typical condo. It is the residential tower of a mixed-use redevelopment of Golden Mile Complex, the first large modern building in Singapore to be conserved. Residents get 188 homes in one 45-storey tower, linked by a Level&nbsp;2 bridge to a refreshed retail, office and medical block. That makes it a <em>scarcity and story</em> play, not a mass-market one.</p>

    <p>It is also now 20 months past launch. Launch weekend was modest: 23 of the 78 first-phase units sold at an average of ~<strong>S$3,005 psf</strong>, which is normal for the Core Central Region (CCR), where projects tend to sell steadily rather than in one weekend. Since then, 2-bedroom units have changed hands at roughly <strong>S$2,770&ndash;2,960 psf</strong> and 3-bedrooms at ~<strong>S$2,650&ndash;3,040 psf</strong>. In plain terms, the price you can negotiate today may sit below the launch average. That is useful to know before you sit down at the sales table.</p>

    <p>Below we walk through the five angles you&rsquo;ll hear from every agent presenting Aurea, then put it through the <a href="/blog/primekey-analysis-introduction">NAVIS PrimeKey Analysis</a> &mdash; the 8-pillar framework we use to grade any Singapore project on data, not on hype.</p>

    <h2>Quick project facts</h2>

    <img src="/assets/images/aurea-logo.png" alt="Aurea project logo" width="640" height="285" style="width:auto; max-width:200px; height:auto; margin:0 0 1.2em; display:block;" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Developer:</strong> GMC Property Pte Ltd &mdash; a joint venture of Perennial Holdings and Far East Organization</li>
      <li><strong>Architect:</strong> DP Architects, who also designed the original Golden Mile Complex; Studio Lapis Conservation as conservation specialist</li>
      <li><strong>Tenure:</strong> 99 years from 18 November 2024 (~97 years remaining)</li>
      <li><strong>Total units:</strong> 188 residential, in one tower of 45 storeys. The conserved block alongside holds a separate 156 office and 19 medical strata units, plus retail &mdash; those are not part of the residential count</li>
      <li><strong>Land area:</strong> 13,462.3&nbsp;sqm (144,908&nbsp;sq&nbsp;ft) for the whole mixed-use site, at a gross plot ratio of 5.6</li>
      <li><strong>District:</strong> D7 &mdash; Beach Road, Downtown Core (Core Central Region, CCR)</li>
      <li><strong>Address:</strong> 802 Beach Road, Singapore 199980 (residential); The Golden Mile at 800 Beach Road, Singapore 199979 (commercial)</li>
      <li><strong>Land cost:</strong> S$700M collective sale in May 2022 for the whole mixed-use site. No separate residential psf ppr has been published, so the figure is context, not a like-for-like land rate</li>
      <li><strong>Nearest MRT:</strong> Nicoll Highway (CC5, Circle Line). The developer&rsquo;s materials put it at ~400&nbsp;m / 5 minutes, which relies on a future connection; the route you can walk today is ~500&nbsp;m / 6 minutes. Lavender (EW11, East-West Line) is ~800&nbsp;m / 9 minutes</li>
      <li><strong>Schools (1&nbsp;km):</strong> none, so there is no Primary 1 ballot advantage at this address. The nearest primaries &mdash; Farrer Park, St Margaret&rsquo;s and Hong Wen &mdash; are about 6 minutes&rsquo; drive</li>
      <li><strong>Car park:</strong> 129 lots plus 3 accessible lots for 188 homes (~0.7 per unit), with 4 EV charging lots and 48 bicycle lots. No visitor lots and no motorcycle lots</li>
      <li><strong>Expected TOP:</strong> Q2 2029 &middot; vacant possession by 31 March 2030</li>
      <li><strong>Indicative maintenance:</strong> from ~S$432/month (2-bedroom) to ~S$612/month (4-Bedroom Premium), subject to final share values</li>
      <li><strong>Sale status:</strong> launched 8 March 2025; selected units available</li>
    </ul>

