    <h3>Where Aurea scores full marks (5&#9733;)</h3>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>GLS / En-bloc Pipeline (5&#9733;).</strong> Five Government Land Sales (GLS) and en-bloc sites within 2&nbsp;km, including Kallang Avenue, Tanjong Rhu Road, Tanjong Rhu Close, Dorset Road and One Sophia. New land at higher prices tends to set new benchmarks for nearby homes. The flip side: those sites also add future supply that will compete for the same buyers.</li>
      <li><strong>Remaining Tenure (5&#9733;).</strong> About 97 years left on a 99-year lease that began in November 2024. Lease decay is not a concern for many years.</li>
      <li><strong>Rental Yield (5&#9733;).</strong> Projected gross yield of 3.42% for the CCR, above the 3% threshold. Supported by tenant demand from the CBD, Bugis and the offices next door at The Golden Mile.</li>
      <li><strong>MOP Cluster (5&#9733;).</strong> The report counts 2,305 HDB units within 2&nbsp;km. That figure is worth unpacking, because the two halves behave differently. <strong>1,681 units</strong> reach MOP between now and 2029 &mdash; Kallang Residences (243 units, Dec 2026), Kallang Breeze (411, Sep 2027), Towner Crest (444, Sep 2028) and Kempas Residences (583, Sep 2029). The other <strong>624</strong> are at Bendemeer Light, which passed MOP in <strong>October 2021</strong>; those owners have already been free to upgrade for five years, and many will have moved. So the genuinely forward-looking upgrader pool here is 1,681, not 2,305 &mdash; still a real source of future private buyers, though at Aurea&rsquo;s quantum many of them will look at cheaper city-fringe options first.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Where it holds its own (3&ndash;4&#9733;)</h3>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>MRT Connectivity (4&#9733;).</strong> A 6-minute walk (~507&nbsp;m) to Nicoll Highway MRT (CC5) at Exit&nbsp;A. Good for daily commutes, but the East-West Line at Lavender is a 9-minute walk, so a two-line household should time both routes.</li>
      <li><strong>Growth Hotspots (4&#9733;).</strong> About 334&nbsp;m from the Kampong Bugis growth area, an 8.2-hectare precinct planned for up to 4,000 homes. Close enough to benefit from new amenities and attention; also close enough to face that supply when you sell.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Where it doesn&rsquo;t (1&ndash;2&#9733;)</h3>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Project Size (2&#9733;).</strong> 188 units. Boutique scale feels private, but fewer units means fewer transactions to set prices and a thinner resale market, especially in a downturn. If you need to sell in a quiet year, a buyer has few comparables to anchor on &mdash; and so do you.</li>
      <li><strong>School Effect (1&#9733;).</strong> No primary school within 1&nbsp;km, so no ballot priority. The nearest primaries (Farrer Park, St Margaret&rsquo;s, Hong Wen) are about 6 minutes&rsquo; drive. A real gap for young families. Remember that 1&nbsp;km only ever gives ballot priority, never a guaranteed place.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>What else to weigh (not scored by PrimeKey)</h3>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>The quantum, not just the psf.</strong> The smallest home here is a 635&nbsp;sq&nbsp;ft 2-bedder, and prices at preview started from ~S$2,750 psf. There is no 1-bedroom entry point, so the cheque is larger than at a comparable city-fringe launch even when the psf looks reasonable.</li>
      <li><strong>Parking is tight, and there are no visitor lots.</strong> About 0.7 lots per home, with nothing set aside for guests and no motorcycle lots. Fine for a car-lite household in the Downtown Core; a constraint if you run two cars or host often.</li>
      <li><strong>You are buying into a working commercial building.</strong> The conserved block next door is a live office, medical and retail address with its own 178 commercial car park lots and its own traffic. That brings convenience on your doorstep and footfall past it. Visit on a weekday, not only on a quiet showflat Sunday.</li>
      <li><strong>Completion is still some way off.</strong> TOP is estimated at Q2 2029, with vacant possession by 31 March 2030. That is a long runway for a 2026 buyer &mdash; useful if you are building up funds, less so if you need somewhere to live sooner.</li>
    </ul>

