    <h2>Who is Aurea actually for?</h2>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>City professionals and couples</strong> working in the CBD, Bugis or Marina Bay who want a 2-bedroom within a short commute and can hold for 7&ndash;10 years.</li>
      <li><strong>Established families upgrading to space</strong> who want a 4-bedroom with a private lift and bay views, and whose children are past the primary-school ballot stage or in international schools nearby.</li>
      <li><strong>Long-horizon investors</strong> who want a scarce, heritage-linked CCR address and are comfortable that the growth catalysts play out over a decade, not a few years.</li>
    </ul>

    <p><strong>Who it doesn&rsquo;t suit:</strong> if you need a primary school within 1&nbsp;km for ballot priority, Aurea has none. If your budget is tight or you may need to sell within 3&ndash;5 years, the quantum and the coming Kampong Bugis supply make a quick, profitable exit uncertain. And if you want two cars or easy visitor parking, ~0.7 lots per unit with no visitor lots is a real constraint.</p>

